name: Screen type
maintainer: unknown
url: https://t.me/Redmi10_Community/310481
note: Check touchscreen type with Device Info HW app (first page, Touchscreen). NVT: mostly safe with any kernel. FTS: needs kernel with new TS/LCM backported or based on new source only (only Niigo and Hydrogen qualify, for now). OMR: no support.
vendor: all

name: Tim Josten IMEI Repair
maintainer: Tim Josten
url: https://graph.org/IMEI-Restoration-05-04
note: Guide to restore/repair IMEI on MediaTek devices with mtk_imei. Fill config.txt, generate imei_repair.zip (Termux or Windows) and flash in recovery or Magisk. Won't work on locked bootloader. Backup NVRAM/NVDATA first.
vendor: all

name: Flash GSI
maintainer: unknown
url: https://t.me/Redmi10Co/23992
note: Guide to flash GSI on selene. Flash vbmeta (all three) with --disable-verity --disable-verification, flash boot (or boot-magisk.img for root), reboot to fastbootd, delete product_a/product_b logical partitions, flash vendor, flash GSI to system, format data in recovery.
vendor: all

name: Flash GSI Termux
maintainer: unknown
url: https://t.me/Redmi10Co/54498
note: Tutorial to flash GSI without a PC. Create folder in storage, extract GSI, rename to system.img, add flash script. Install termux-adb-fastboot if needed (curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/offici5l/termux-adb-fastboot/main/install | bash). Boot to fastbootd, termux-setup-storage, chmod +x FLASH_GSI.sh && bash FLASH_GSI.sh. Phone reboots to recovery, format data and reboot.
vendor: all
